<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p><h1 class="research-title">49 BCE</h1><p class="ref-lede">49 BCE in world history: 7 events and 2 deaths. 180 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/133-bce">133 BCE</a><a href="/years/63-bce">63 BCE</a><a href="/years/54-bce">54 BCE</a><a href="/years/51-bce">51 BCE</a><a href="/years/49-bce" aria-current="page">49 BCE</a><a href="/years/48-bce">48 BCE</a><a href="/years/46-bce">46 BCE</a><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a><a href="/years/43-bce">43 BCE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-7">7 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Caesar's tribunes are driven from Rome and flee to Ravenna</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Senate's hardliners rejected Caesar's offer that he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> both disarm, the tribunes who supported him were driven from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and fled to Caesar at Ravenna. The Senate then declared Caesar an enemy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-10">10 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar crosses the Rubicon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Leading a legion across the small river that marked the border of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, Caesar defied the Senate and made civil war inevitable. 'The die is cast', he reportedly said. The war ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-2">2 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pompey's legates Afranius and Petreius surrender to Caesar at Ilerda</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After early successes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legatus">legates</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-petreius">Marcus Petreius</a> and Lucius Afranius, were forced to capitulate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Ilerda</a> and disband their army. Caesar let them go free, and they travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> to join Pompey.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-petreius">Marcus Petreius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juba-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-24">24 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Juba I and the Pompeians destroy Curio's army on the Bagradas</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a>, the Pompeians under Publius Attius Varus and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I of Numidia</a> routed the army of Caesar's general Gaius Scribonius Curio near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medjerda">Bagradas</a> River, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. Curio was killed in the battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/crossing-of-the-rubicon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crossing-of-the-rubicon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/crossing-of-the-rubicon">Crossing of the Rubicon</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The crossing of the Rubicon was Julius Caesar's decision in 49 BCE to lead his army across the Rubicon River in northern Italy, the boundary of his province, in defiance of the Senate.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ilerda">Battle of Ilerda</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Ilerda was Julius Caesar's campaign of June to August 49 BCE near modern Lleida in north-eastern Spain against the Pompeian legates Afranius and Petreius, at the start of his civil war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-bagradas-river-49-bce">Battle of the Bagradas River (49 BCE)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of the Bagradas River was fought in August 49 BCE in the province of Africa, near the river now called the Medjerda in Tunisia.</p></div></li></ol></section>
